    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work the body as an oval in alternating yellow and black stripes using "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "stripe-carry-a92"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "stripe carry"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Each stripe is 2 rounds. Insert "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "safety-eye-a92"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "safety eyes"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " between rounds 5 and 6 before stuffing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Body (14 rounds): 4.5 cm oval."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Wings (make 2, 7 rounds each): small 2 cm oval in off-white or cream. Leave a long tail for attachment."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stinger (6 rounds): small cone in black. Sew to the pointed end of the body."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stripes"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Rounds 1 to 2: yellow. Rounds 3 to 4: black. Rounds 5 to 6: yellow. Rounds 7 to 8: black. Continue pattern until body is complete. Use "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "stripe-carry-a92"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "stripe carry"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " throughout."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Wings"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work two small oval wings in cream. Do not stuff. Flatten slightly and sew to the top of the body, angling outward at 45 degrees."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Assembly"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sew stinger to back. Sew wings to the centre top. Embroider antennae with a length of black yarn, knotting each tip."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
